---
import DevLayout from 'kp-design/layouts/DevLayout.astro';
---

<DevLayout title="Accessibility" description="How kylepace.dev and its experiments are built to work for everyone.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>
    <p>
      Every experiment here aims for the same standard as <a href="https://kylepace.net/accessibility/">kylepace.net</a>:
      WCAG 2.2 AA, Atkinson Hyperlegible type, readable contrast in light and dark mode, full keyboard support, and motion
      only when your device allows it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Experiments are works in progress, so some will fall short while they’re being built. Interactive pieces like maps
      and visualizations are the hardest to get right, and each one says in text what it shows.
    </p>
    <h2>Display settings</h2>
    <p>
      The round button in the corner of every page lets you change theme, text size, contrast, font, spacing, motion and
      link underlines. Your choices are saved in this browser for kylepace.dev. Because it’s a separate site, settings
      from kylepace.net don’t carry over, so you may need to set them once here too.
    </p>
    <h2>Tell me what’s not working</h2>
    <p>
      If something gets in your way,
      <a href="mailto:mail@kylepace.net?subject=Accessibility%20on%20kylepace.dev">email me</a> with the page and what
      happened, and I’ll aim to reply within a week.
    </p>
  </article>
</DevLayout>

<style>
  article {
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
</style>
